IMPORT prelude

-- Education Act 1957 (Singapore) -- what counts as a school and when it must be registered (ss 2, 3, 4, 21), the restriction on
-- calling yourself a "school" or "academy" (s 4A), refusal and cancellation of a school's registration (ss 24, 25), the size of a
-- committee of management (s 26(2)), who may teach and the grounds for refusing or cancelling a teacher's registration or authority
-- (ss 35, 38, 39, 40, 42, 43), the 14-day appeal and whether it goes to the Minister or the Schools Appeals Board (ss 15, 47, 48),
-- the effect of cancelling a school (ss 49(1), 50), and penalties (ss 4A(3), 17, 62, 64).
--
-- Edition: 2020 Revised Edition, informal consolidation, as deposited at ../../registers/source-bundle/EA1957.txt, with amendments to
-- Act 5 of 2025 (in force 9 March 2025) shown.
--
-- WHY THIS ACT. Cited by 9 of the 527 Singapore Acts deposited in this repository. SCOPED to the decisions a school operator, a
-- teacher, or someone naming an education business actually meets. Not encoded: the Education Finance Board and the Educational
-- Advisory Council (Parts 2 and 3), the constitution and procedure of the Appeals Board (ss 13, 14, 16, 18), registration of
-- supervisors and managers beyond the appeal route (ss 28-34), inspection and search powers (ss 51-55), appeal hearing procedure
-- (ss 56-60) beyond s 58's onus, regulations (s 61), service (s 63), savings (s 66) and the Schedule forms.
--
-- The ARRANGEMENT OF SECTIONS at the top of the deposit is numbered out of step with the body (it lists "Exemption" as s 1 and
-- "Appeal to be argued on grounds stated" as s 59). This encoding follows the BODY's numbers throughout.
--
-- NAIVE ENCODING. Straight from the deposited text with the writing-l4-rules skill. No pipeline, no coverage table,
-- no independent test pass, no human gate. See NOTES.md.

§ `Education Act 1957 -- schools and teachers`

§§ `2, 3, 4, 21 -- what is a school, and must it be registered`

-- s 2: "school" means "(a) an organisation for the provision of education for 10 or more persons; or (b) a place where 10 or more
-- persons are being or are habitually taught".
-- s 3: the Minister may by Gazette notification exempt a school whose teaching "is of a purely religious character" or which "is an
-- institution of higher education".
-- s 4: "This Act shall not apply" to (a) the Institute of Technical Education, (b) "any private education institution within the
-- meaning of the Private Education Act 2009", (c) "any early childhood development centre licensed under the Early Childhood
-- Development Centres Act 2017".
-- s 21: "Subject to section 3, no school shall be carried on unless it is registered under this Act." s 22(1): the Director-General
-- shall cause every Government school to be registered -- so Government schools are registered too.
DECLARE Institution IS ONE OF
    `an ordinary school`
    `a Government school`
    `the Institute of Technical Education`
    `a private education institution`
    `a licensed early childhood development centre`

GIVEN `persons taught` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `it is a school` IF `persons taught` AT LEAST 10

GIVEN `the institution` IS AN Institution
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Act applies` IF
    CONSIDER `the institution`
    WHEN `the Institute of Technical Education` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a private education institution` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `a licensed early childhood development centre` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the institution` IS AN Institution, `persons taught` IS A NUMBER, `exempted by the Minister` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `registration under this Act is required` IF
    `it is a school` `persons taught` AND `the Act applies` `the institution` AND (NOT `exempted by the Minister`)

§§ `4A -- calling yourself a school, academy, college or university`

-- s 4A(1): no person or organisation shall, "except with the written consent of the Director-General", use "academy", "college",
-- "school", "university" (or a Gazetted term, or any derivative, in any language) in the name under which it is providing education.
-- (2) does not apply to (a) "a school that is registered or exempted from registration under this Act"; (b) the Government; (c) a
-- body established under a public Act with a public function, or its wholly-owned entity; (d) an education institution established
-- by or functioning under any other written law; (e) prescribed persons. (3): fine up to $2,000, imprisonment up to 12 months, or both.
--
-- INFERENCE, not in s 4A's text: a private education institution is not listed in s 4A(2), but s 4 says the whole Act "shall not
-- apply" to it, so it is treated here as outside s 4A.
DECLARE NameUser IS ONE OF
    `a registered or exempted school`
    `the Government`
    `a statutory body with a public function`
    `an education institution under another written law`
    `a prescribed person`
    `a PEI under the Private Education Act 2009`
    `a tuition business`

GIVEN `the user` IS A NameUser
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the user is outside section 4A` IF
    CONSIDER `the user`
    WHEN `a tuition business` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE TRUE

GIVEN `the user` IS A NameUser, `uses an education word in its name` IS A BOOLEAN, `has the Director-General's written consent` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `using the name is an offence` IF
    `uses an education word in its name` AND (NOT `has the Director-General's written consent`) AND (NOT `the user is outside section 4A` `the user`)

§§ `24, 25 -- refusing and cancelling a school's registration`

-- s 24: the Director-General may refuse to register a school if, among 18 grounds, "(a) adequate educational facilities already exist
-- in the area"; "(b) ... dangerous building ... structurally unsuitable"; "(c) the fire precautions ... are inadequate"; "(g) the
-- proposed fees are excessive"; "(j) the proposed school is designed to accommodate more than 1,200 pupils in any one session";
-- "(m) the proposed school has previously been refused registration or the registration thereof has been cancelled"; "(p) ... likely
-- to be used as a meeting place of an unlawful society"; "(r) ... a statement ... false in a material particular".
-- s 25(1): the Director-General may cancel registration "(a) on any of the grounds on which he would have been entitled to refuse
-- registration under section 24, OTHER THAN that set out in paragraph (a) thereof"; (b) the school has ceased to exist; (c) the
-- supervisor has failed to comply with a s 54 direction; (d) the committee is not efficiently administering the school; (e)
-- "discipline in the school has not been or cannot be adequately maintained".
-- s 25(2): if the registration of ALL the managers has been cancelled, the Director-General SHALL cancel the school's registration.
DECLARE SchoolGround IS ONE OF
    `adequate facilities already exist in the area`
    `the premises are dangerous or structurally unsuitable`
    `the fire precautions are inadequate`
    `the fees are excessive`
    `it is designed for more than 1,200 pupils in a session`
    `it was previously refused or cancelled`
    `it is likely to be a meeting place of an unlawful society`
    `the application contained a false statement`
    `the school has ceased to exist`
    `the supervisor ignored a remedial direction`
    `the committee is not administering efficiently`
    `discipline cannot be maintained`
    `the school's popularity has fallen`

GIVEN `pupils per session` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the capacity exceeds the limit` IF `pupils per session` GREATER THAN 1200

GIVEN `the ground` IS A SchoolGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a section 24 ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `adequate facilities already exist in the area` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the premises are dangerous or structurally unsuitable` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the fire precautions are inadequate` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the fees are excessive` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it is designed for more than 1,200 pupils in a session` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it was previously refused or cancelled` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `it is likely to be a meeting place of an unlawful society` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the application contained a false statement` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A SchoolGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may refuse to register the school` IF `is a section 24 ground` `the ground`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A SchoolGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may cancel the school's registration` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `adequate facilities already exist in the area` THEN FALSE
    WHEN `the school has ceased to exist` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the supervisor ignored a remedial direction` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the committee is not administering efficiently` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `discipline cannot be maintained` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE `is a section 24 ground` `the ground`

GIVEN `managers on the register` IS A NUMBER, `managers whose registration was cancelled` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General must cancel the school's registration` IF
    `managers on the register` GREATER THAN 0 AND `managers whose registration was cancelled` AT LEAST `managers on the register`

§§ `26(2) -- size of the committee of management`

-- s 26(2): "Except with the approval in writing of the Director-General, no committee of management shall exceed 9 persons in number."
GIVEN `committee members` IS A NUMBER, `has written approval` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the committee is lawfully constituted in size` IF
    `committee members` AT MOST 9 OR `has written approval`

§§ `20, 35, 40, 44 -- who may teach`

-- s 35: "No person shall teach or be employed as a teacher in a school other than a school exempted from the provisions of this Act
-- unless he is either a registered teacher or is authorised or permitted to teach under Part 9."
-- s 40(1): an unregistered teacher may teach only if an authority (s 41) or a permit (s 44) has been issued.
-- s 44(1): the Director-General may "in his discretion and for special reasons issue a permit to any person to teach as an
-- unregistered teacher" -- "Notwithstanding anything in this Act".
-- s 20(c): it is an offence to teach "in an unregistered school" or in a registered school without registration, authority or permit.
GIVEN `the school is registered` IS A BOOLEAN, `the school is exempted` IS A BOOLEAN, `is a registered teacher` IS A BOOLEAN,
      `holds an authority to teach` IS A BOOLEAN, `holds a permit to teach` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the person may lawfully teach there` IF
        `the school is exempted`
    OR  (`the school is registered` AND (`is a registered teacher` OR `holds an authority to teach` OR `holds a permit to teach`))

§§ `38, 39, 42, 43 -- refusing and cancelling teachers`

-- s 38: the Director-General may refuse to register a teacher who (a) "is not of good character"; (b) has a conviction for an offence
-- punishable with imprisonment; (c) was previously refused; (d) "has been struck off the register ... unless the cancellation ... has
-- taken place because of his resignation or because the school in which he was employed has ceased to exist"; (e) cannot show medical
-- fitness; (f) made a false statement; (g) "is likely to influence his pupils in a manner prejudicial to their welfare or to the
-- public interest"; or (h) "does not possess the minimum qualifications prescribed in the regulations".
-- s 39: may cancel (a) on any s 38 ground; (b) "professional misconduct"; (c) "not competent"; (d) contravention of the Act.
-- s 42: may refuse to authorise an unregistered teacher (a) on the grounds in "section 38(a) to (g)" -- NOT (h); or (b) "if there is
-- available for employment in the school concerned a suitable registered teacher".
-- s 43(1): may cancel the authority (a) on any ground on which he could cancel registration under s 39 -- which by s 39(a) includes
-- s 38(h); or (b) "if a registered teacher with the required qualifications becomes available". (2): SHALL cancel when the authorised
-- employment is terminated.
DECLARE TeacherGround IS ONE OF
    `not of good character`
    `convicted of an imprisonable offence`
    `previously refused registration`
    `struck off for misconduct`
    `struck off only because of resignation or the school ceasing`
    `cannot show medical fitness`
    `made a false statement`
    `likely to influence pupils prejudicially`
    `lacks the prescribed minimum qualifications`
    `guilty of professional misconduct`
    `not competent`
    `contravened the Act`
    `a suitable registered teacher is available`
    `a qualified registered teacher has become available`
    `the authorised employment has ended`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A TeacherGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a section 38(a) to (g) ground` IF
    CONSIDER `the ground`
    WHEN `not of good character` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `convicted of an imprisonable offence` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `previously refused registration` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `struck off for misconduct` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cannot show medical fitness` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `made a false statement` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `likely to influence pupils prejudicially` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the ground` IS A TeacherGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may refuse to register the teacher` IF
    `is a section 38(a) to (g) ground` `the ground` OR `the ground` EQUALS `lacks the prescribed minimum qualifications`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A TeacherGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may cancel the teacher's registration` IF
        `the Director-General may refuse to register the teacher` `the ground`
    OR  `the ground` EQUALS `guilty of professional misconduct`
    OR  `the ground` EQUALS `not competent`
    OR  `the ground` EQUALS `contravened the Act`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A TeacherGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may refuse to authorise an unregistered teacher` IF
    `is a section 38(a) to (g) ground` `the ground` OR `the ground` EQUALS `a suitable registered teacher is available`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A TeacherGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General may cancel the authority to teach` IF
        `the Director-General may cancel the teacher's registration` `the ground`
    OR  `the ground` EQUALS `a qualified registered teacher has become available`
    OR  `the ground` EQUALS `the authorised employment has ended`

GIVEN `the ground` IS A TeacherGround
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Director-General must cancel the authority to teach` IF `the ground` EQUALS `the authorised employment has ended`

§§ `15, 47, 48, 58 -- appeals`

-- s 48(2): a person adversely affected "may within 14 days of the service of the notice appeal ... (a) in cases where the decision has
-- been made under section 24(n), (o) or (p), 25(1)(a) or (e), 33(f), 34(f) or (g), 38(g) or 39(a) to the Minister; (b) in all other
-- cases to the Appeals Board"; "Provided that the Minister may direct that any appeal made to him shall be heard by the Appeals Board."
-- s 47: an applicant may appeal against conditions of registration "within 14 days of the receipt of the notice" to the Appeals Board.
-- s 54(3): a supervisor may appeal against a remedial direction to the Appeals Board within the time for compliance.
-- s 15 proviso: the Appeals Board "shall not hear an appeal from any Government teacher other than an appeal against the cancellation
-- of his registration as a teacher".
-- s 58: "The onus of proving that the grounds stated by the Director-General ... are not correct or do not justify such decision shall
-- be upon the appellant." s 60(3): the decision on appeal is "final and conclusive and shall not be questioned in any court".
--
-- s 25(1)(a) cancels a school on any s 24 ground, and s 39(a) cancels a teacher on any s 38 ground. Because s 48(2)(a) names 25(1)(a)
-- and 39(a) wholesale, a cancellation on (say) fire precautions or qualifications goes to the MINISTER, while a refusal on the same
-- ground goes to the APPEALS BOARD.
DECLARE Decision IS ONE OF
    `refusing a school for unsafe premises`
    `refusing a school for inadequate fire precautions`
    `refusing a school as a likely unlawful-society meeting place`
    `cancelling a school for inadequate fire precautions`
    `cancelling a school because discipline cannot be maintained`
    `cancelling a school that has ceased to exist`
    `imposing conditions on a school's registration`
    `refusing a manager as not of good character`
    `refusing a manager as prejudicial to the public interest`
    `cancelling a manager who is evading responsibilities`
    `refusing a teacher lacking minimum qualifications`
    `refusing a teacher likely to influence pupils prejudicially`
    `cancelling a teacher for lacking minimum qualifications`
    `cancelling a teacher for professional misconduct`
    `refusing authority for an unregistered teacher`
    `directing remedial measures`

DECLARE Forum IS ONE OF
    `the Minister`
    `the Appeals Board`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A Forum
`the appeal lies to` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `refusing a school as a likely unlawful-society meeting place` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `cancelling a school for inadequate fire precautions` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `cancelling a school because discipline cannot be maintained` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `refusing a manager as prejudicial to the public interest` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `cancelling a manager who is evading responsibilities` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `refusing a teacher likely to influence pupils prejudicially` THEN `the Minister`
    WHEN `cancelling a teacher for lacking minimum qualifications` THEN `the Minister`
    OTHERWISE `the Appeals Board`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `the Minister directs the Board to hear it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A Forum
`the appeal is heard by` MEANS
    IF `the Minister directs the Board to hear it` THEN `the Appeals Board` ELSE `the appeal lies to` `the decision`

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `is a cancellation of a teacher's registration` IF
    CONSIDER `the decision`
    WHEN `cancelling a teacher for lacking minimum qualifications` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `cancelling a teacher for professional misconduct` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the decision` IS A Decision, `the appellant is a Government teacher` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the Appeals Board may hear the appeal` IF
    `the appeal lies to` `the decision` EQUALS `the Appeals Board`
    AND ((NOT `the appellant is a Government teacher`) OR `is a cancellation of a teacher's registration` `the decision`)

GIVEN `days since service of the notice` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the appeal is in time` IF `days since service of the notice` AT MOST 14

§§ `49(1), 50 -- after a school's registration is cancelled`

-- s 49(1): a cancelled school "shall cease to be carried on with effect from the date of service of notice under section 48", unless
-- the Director-General by notice "permit[s] the school to be carried on until the determination of any appeal".
-- s 50: where the registration is cancelled and the school has not been permitted to carry on, "it shall be an offence for any pupil
-- of the school or for any other person without the written authority of the Director-General to be or to assemble on the premises",
-- and police may enter using necessary force.
GIVEN `registration cancelled` IS A BOOLEAN, `permitted to carry on pending appeal` IS A BOOLEAN, `has written authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `being on the premises is an offence` IF
    `registration cancelled` AND (NOT `permitted to carry on pending appeal`) AND (NOT `has written authority`)

§§ `4A(3), 17, 62, 64 -- penalties`

-- s 62(1): (a) acting as manager or teacher of an unregistered, unexempted school; (b) a knowingly or recklessly false statement in
-- an application; (c) obstructing an inspection; (d) refusing to produce documents under s 53; (e) acting as manager or teacher
-- without registration, authority or permit; (f) continuing to act after cancellation -- "a fine not exceeding $2,000 or ...
-- imprisonment for a term not exceeding one year or ... both".
-- s 62(2): an offence "for which no other penalty is specifically provided" -- "a fine not exceeding $500 for a first offence or
-- $1,000 for a second or subsequent offence", and a manager or teacher convicted under "section 20 or 23(3)" is liable to "a further
-- fine not exceeding $100 for every day during which the offence continues after conviction". No imprisonment.
-- s 4A(3): $2,000 or 12 months or both. s 17: a summoned witness who fails to attend or answer -- $500 or 3 months or both.
-- s 61(3): a manager or teacher who commits or abets a breach of the regulations "whether directly or through negligence" is guilty
-- of an offence (penalty from s 62(2)).
-- s 64: "No person shall be charged with any offence under this Act ... except on the complaint of the Director-General."
--
-- INFERENCE: s 23(3) (exhibiting the certificate and list of staff) does not itself say it is an offence; s 62(2) speaks of an
-- "offence under section ... 23(3)", so a breach of it is treated here as one carrying the s 62(2) penalty.
DECLARE Offence IS ONE OF
    `using an education name without consent`
    `failing to attend or answer as a witness`
    `acting as manager of an unregistered school`
    `a false statement in an application`
    `obstructing an inspection`
    `teaching without registration, authority or permit`
    `employing an unregistered teacher without authority`
    `failing to exhibit the certificate of registration`
    `being on the premises of a cancelled school`
    `a breach of the regulations`

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `falls under section 62(1)` IF
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `acting as manager of an unregistered school` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `a false statement in an application` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `obstructing an inspection` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `teaching without registration, authority or permit` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `previously convicted under this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum fine` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using an education name without consent` THEN 2000
    WHEN `failing to attend or answer as a witness` THEN 500
    OTHERWISE
        IF `falls under section 62(1)` `the offence`
        THEN 2000
        ELSE IF `previously convicted under this Act` THEN 1000 ELSE 500

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum imprisonment in months` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the offence`
    WHEN `using an education name without consent` THEN 12
    WHEN `failing to attend or answer as a witness` THEN 3
    OTHERWISE
        IF `falls under section 62(1)` `the offence` THEN 12 ELSE 0

GIVEN `the offence` IS AN Offence, `the offender is a manager or teacher` IS A BOOLEAN, `days continuing after conviction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the maximum continuing fine` MEANS
    IF `the offender is a manager or teacher`
       AND (`the offence` EQUALS `employing an unregistered teacher without authority` OR `the offence` EQUALS `failing to exhibit the certificate of registration`)
    THEN 100 TIMES `days continuing after conviction`
    ELSE 0

GIVEN `the Director-General complained` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `a charge may be brought` IF `the Director-General complained`
